---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

/**
 * Canonical public face of Identity Engineering OS.
 * Framework = geometry + living scaffold.
 * OS = usable system that operationalizes every layer.
 * Space is one: physics (degrees of freedom) + biology (boundary) in one installable host.
 * /method redirects here for legacy URLs.
 */
const osRepo = 'https://github.com/identity-engineering/os';
const osSpaceModel = 'https://github.com/identity-engineering/os/blob/main/docs/space-model.md';
const osAccountIdentity = 'https://github.com/identity-engineering/os/blob/main/docs/account-identity-model.md';
const osCreationJurisdiction =
	'https://github.com/identity-engineering/os/blob/main/docs/identity-creation-jurisdiction.md';
const skillCoachUrl = '/skills/identity-engineer';
const skillContributorUrl = '/skills/identity-engineer-contributor';
---

<Layout title="OS | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="border-b border-white/10 px-6 pt-28 pb-16">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
				<div class="mb-4 text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">OS</div>
				<h1 class="text-5xl font-bold tracking-tighter text-white md:text-6xl leading-[0.95]">
					Install the framework as a living system.
				</h1>
				<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xl font-light leading-relaxed text-white/50">
					Identity Engineering OS is the practical, file-based runtime of the framework.
					Not a separate product shelf: the place where Single, Interactive, Collective, and Living layers become operable artifacts.
				</p>
				<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
					<a
						href={osRepo}
						class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer"
					>Open OS repository →</a>
					<a
						href="/framework"
						class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition"
					>Framework map</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-6 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">Framework and OS</h2>
				<p>
					<strong class="text-white/85">Framework</strong> holds the conceptual map:
					geometry (Single · Interactive · Collective) and the operational scaffold of Living Identity.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong class="text-white/85">OS</strong> is the installable system that turns that map into files, signals, receipts, and local runtime.
					Every layer is operationalized, not only Living. Living is the lens that says how geometry is metabolized;
					the OS is where all four layers become usable.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-6 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">Operational units</h2>
				<p>
					These units are how OS names the geometry and membrane of the framework without inventing a second ontology.
				</p>
				<div class="space-y-4">
					<article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/20 p-5">
						<div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35 mb-2">Space</div>
						<p class="text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
							<strong class="text-white/90">One Space.</strong>
							Physics: arena of degrees of freedom
							(<a href="/framework/space" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Space</a>).
							Biology: membrane and selective exchange
							(<a href="/framework/boundary" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Boundary</a>).
							OS: installable host of Identities with membership, Surface, and membrane policy.
							A local Free install is a mini-Space; managed continuity is the same geometry under a hosted Space.
							When the Space is an emergent collective Identity, its outer membrane is that Identity's Boundary; members keep theirs under
							<a href="/framework/multicellularity" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Multicellularity</a>.
						</p>
					</article>
					<article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/20 p-5">
						<div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35 mb-2">Identity</div>
						<p class="text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
							Geometric unit: Stem, Registry, Mass, Surface, Public Card, signals.
							Human, agent, idea, org, and runtime substrates share the same contracts.
							Harnesses bind to an Identity; they are not anonymous account modes.
						</p>
					</article>
					<article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/20 p-5">
						<div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35 mb-2">Identity creation</div>
						<p class="text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
							Creating an Identity records factual lineage and issues a default jurisdiction package: transferable grants for policy, visibility, Surface, and grant admin.
							Ordinary Parent grants are revocable by the Child. A narrow residual emergency lever (freeze, quarantine, visibility re-evaluation) remains for the creator line; it is audited and is not full admin over the Child Stem.
							<strong class="text-white/90">Known is not addressable by default:</strong> registration in a Space does not imply Surface reachability.
							Biology-lens reading:
							<a href="/framework/gene" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Gene</a>.
						</p>
					</article>
					<article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/20 p-5">
						<div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35 mb-2">Account ≠ Identity</div>
						<p class="text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
							An IE Account is auth and plan on the IE product. Geometry lives only on Identities.
							Local Free geometry does not require an account.
						</p>
					</article>
					<article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/20 p-5">
						<div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35 mb-2">Registry</div>
						<p class="text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
							Always observer-relative: each Identity's perception of others.
							Registry is not the Space host and not a shared team perception store.
						</p>
					</article>
				</div>
				<p class="text-sm text-white/45">
					Open Core contracts:
					<a href={osSpaceModel} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-white/70 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">space-model.md</a>
					·
					<a href={osAccountIdentity} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-white/70 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">account-identity-model.md</a>
					·
					<a href={osCreationJurisdiction} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-white/70 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">identity-creation-jurisdiction.md</a>
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-6 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-8">How the layers land in the OS</h2>
				<div class="space-y-6">
					<article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] p-5">
						<div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35 mb-2">01 · Single</div>
						<p class="text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
							<strong class="text-white/90">Stem, Mass, Curvature, Rotation</strong> → local Stem files, Metric Stem, Registry self-perception,
							Header / local entry as always-on State Differential + Vision Gradient.
						</p>
					</article>
					<article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] p-5">
						<div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35 mb-2">02 · Interactive</div>
						<p class="text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
							<strong class="text-white/90">Gravitation, Relativity, Frequency</strong> → Interaction Signal, foreign-estimate zone,
							bidirectional estimate requests, consent policy at the Surface.
						</p>
					</article>
					<article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] p-5">
						<div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35 mb-2">03 · Collective</div>
						<p class="text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
							<strong class="text-white/90">Emergence, Multicellularity, Damping</strong> → multi-identity coupling over Signals and shared consented context;
							collective contracts grow on the same Surface standard (not a separate social platform).
							A Space as collective form has its own Boundary; member Identities keep theirs.
						</p>
					</article>
					<article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] p-5">
						<div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[3px] text-white/35 mb-2">04 · Living</div>
						<p class="text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
							<strong class="text-white/90">Boundary, Metabolism, IE operating cycle, Organism</strong> → Surface as membrane; Geometry Receipt by default after a non-rejected Interact apply;
							<strong class="text-white/90">Think</strong> as phase label (substrate plan-mode / private memory / prompts, no IE CLI);
							<strong class="text-white/90">Interact</strong> as tools, APIs, MCPs, signals, deterministic scripts;
							<strong class="text-white/90">Mature</strong> as directed self-evolve (<code class="text-white/80">ie mature</code> → Geometry Receipt, optional ownership_move record only).
							Cell-biology lens on the form without importing organism agents.
						</p>
					</article>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-6 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">Core runtime loop</h2>
				<p>
					Under Relativity every act is Interaction. The OS default path:
				</p>
				<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 text-white/70">
					<li><strong class="text-white/90">Interact</strong>: Interaction Signal or tool path crosses the Surface; policy gates the foreign-estimate zone.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-white/90">Geometry Receipt</strong> is extracted by default after a non-rejected Interact apply: relative mass proxies, tension components, continuity hints.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-white/90">Mature</strong> (optional, deliberate): <code class="text-white/80">ie mature</code> records directed causal integration of the own Trajectory as a self Geometry Receipt; ownership_move stays on the receipt until Ownership design applies it.</li>
					<li>Receipts live under the local registry. Continuous write-back into live Tensor, Tension, and Registry alloys is the next OS heartbeat (not automatic yet).</li>
				</ol>
				<p class="text-white/50">
					Think is not a separate runtime step in the OS: it is the inward, non-emitting phase provided by the substrate and named under Relativity.
					That is Probes-as-Bridge in practice: measurement and potential reshape in one process.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-6 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white">Get it running</h2>
				<p>
					Personal-first, local-first. Clone the OS, initialize a registry, apply signals, run Mature when the Trajectory needs a directed record.
					Public release packages (brew / versioned installs under the org domain) are on the roadmap.
				</p>
				<pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/40 p-4 text-sm text-white/80 leading-relaxed"><code># Conceptual path (see OS repo README for current commands)
git clone https://github.com/identity-engineering/os.git
cd os
# ie init · ie signal apply · ie mature · registry under templates/personal/</code></pre>
				<p class="text-sm text-white/45">
					Exact CLI flags and release channels evolve in the OS repo. This page is the public orientation;
					the repository is the source of truth for install steps.
				</p>
				<a
					href={osRepo}
					class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-white/80 hover:text-white border-b border-white/25 hover:border-white/50 pb-0.5 transition"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>identity-engineering/os on GitHub →</a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-6 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">What this is not</h2>
				<ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
					<li>Not a global social network or attention platform.</li>
					<li>Not a full organism-agent suite (sensory / immunity / … modules stay out until Framework-derived).</li>
					<li>Not a Think isolation runtime: protected inward work is substrate-provided.</li>
					<li>Not therapy, diagnosis, or a claim of physical law.</li>
					<li>Not a replacement for the geometric Core Concepts: OS implements them.</li>
					<li>Not a second Space ontology: OS Space is the framework Space made installable.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-6 py-16">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
				<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">Optional: agent skills</h2>
				<p class="text-white/50 leading-relaxed mb-6">
					Dialogue skills for coaching and contribution quality remain available.
					They are helpers around the framework, not the OS itself.
				</p>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
					<a href={skillCoachUrl} class="px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full border border-white/15 text-sm text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Identity Engineer skill</a>
					<a href={skillContributorUrl} class="px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full border border-white/15 text-sm text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Contributor skill</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
